# Build context policy — deny by default.
#
# Every image builds with the repository root as its context, because each
# service has a path dependency on libs/domain and a narrower context could not
# see it. Without this file the whole tree is sent to the Docker daemon or a
# remote builder on every build: hundreds of megabytes of virtualenvs and
# node_modules, the entire .git history, and — the reason this is a security
# control and not a speed optimisation — anything sitting in a gitignored
# uploads or /data directory.
#
# `.gitignore` does not apply to a build context. A file being untracked says
# nothing about whether Docker will ship it.
#
# So: exclude everything, then re-include exactly what a build needs. A new
# service directory has to be added here deliberately, which is the point.

*

# --- what the images actually need -------------------------------------------
!libs/domain/pyproject.toml
!libs/domain/src/
!libs/test-support/pyproject.toml
!libs/test-support/src/

!services/core-api/pyproject.toml
!services/core-api/uv.lock
!services/core-api/src/

!services/blind-svc/pyproject.toml
!services/blind-svc/uv.lock
!services/blind-svc/src/

!services/extraction-svc/pyproject.toml
!services/extraction-svc/uv.lock
!services/extraction-svc/src/

!services/render-svc/pyproject.toml
!services/render-svc/uv.lock
!services/render-svc/src/

# --- re-excluded even inside the allowed paths --------------------------------
# The `!` rules above are directory-wide, so anything that could hide under
# them is denied again here.
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/tests/
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Client data must never reach a build context, even by accident.
**/*.pdf
**/*.docx
**/*.seed
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/uploads/
**/inbox/
data/
